Server log (auth.otp.* lines during the walkthrough): request outcome=sent / delivery outcome=delivered per
"Send code"; verify outcome=ok for steps 7 and the earlier single-request run.

Automation note (recorded so the evidence is read correctly)
- One verify in an early run answered "mismatch" with an empty gu/domain, i.e. no pending challenge in the
  session. The server log shows why: between that run's second request (16:43:43Z) and its verify
  (16:44:01Z) a logout.do (16:43:56Z) that the walkthrough did not issue, preceded by a superadmin (user 1082)
  session on superadmin/marloParameters.do (16:42:43Z-16:43:06Z). The user was using the same local app in the
  same browser profile at the same time; the shared localhost cookie made that logout end the walkthrough's
  session. Not a T17 defect. Repeated afterwards with curl (two sequences), with fetch from the page, and
  with the page handlers (step 7): all ok.
- Later in the session the automation's key events stopped reaching the page (a capturing keydown listener
  recorded 0 events after a Return), so Enter results taken by real key presses in that window were
  discarded and step 8 was re-measured with dispatched events instead. A dispatched event proves the guard
  cancels the keydown; it does not trigger the browser's implicit form submission, so the end-to-end
  "Enter on the checkbox does not POST login.do" remains proven by the guard plus the code review, not by a
  trusted key press. Recorded as a limit, not a pass.

Not covered here: screen-reader behaviour (accepted gap, requirements section 6).
